    "result": "`search_products` is implemented in `solution.py`, and all 14 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass. I did not run a coverage report, so the 90% coverage gate is unchecked. The tests exercise every branch of the function, so I expect it to clear.\n\nThe function builds one parameterized SELECT. The substring match uses `instr(lower(name), lower(?))`, so `%` and `_` are plain characters and matching is case-insensitive for ASCII only. Ties are broken by `id` ascending whichever way the main order runs.\n\nIt raises `ValueError` for a bad `order_by`, a `limit` outside 1–100 or an `offset` below 0. I made it also reject non-integer values for `limit` and `offset`, including booleans, which the spec doesn't mention.\n\nThe tests cover the stock filter, the result keys, case-insensitive matching, literal `%` and `_`, `max_price`, ordering and tie-breaks, `limit`/`offset`, and the invalid-argument cases.",
